    <title>
        ci(proof-profile): free runner disk before restoring caches (#760)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T17:35:13Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17322558?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>Vilin97</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/Vilin97</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;ci(proof-profile): free runner disk before restoring caches (#760)

The measure and absolute jobs ran out of space in &amp;quot;Restore pool build&amp;quot;
(System.IO.IOException: No space left on device), so every profile
comment came back empty. Add the same &amp;quot;Free runner disk space&amp;quot; step
main CI already uses, before the dependency and pool-build restores.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/49bdad2b2b82b4b41d75a8e251ac10b2aa08fb45</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/LeanPool/lean-pool/commit/49bdad2b2b82b4b41d75a8e251ac10b2aa08fb45"/>
    <title>
        Make every Lean warning a compile error (warningAsError, like Tau Cet…
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T17:43:31Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17322558?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>Vilin97</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/Vilin97</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Make every Lean warning a compile error (warningAsError, like Tau Ceti) (#751)

* Make every Lean warning a compile error

Set `warningAsError = true` in the package&amp;#39;s leanOptions, as Tau Ceti
does. CI already rejected warnings by scanning the build log; this moves
the rule into the compiler, so local `lake build` fails the same way and
a cached build can no longer hide a warning (a warning now means no
.olean). Pool files cannot opt out because `set_option` is banned by the
quality gate. The log scan stays for warnings Lake itself prints.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;

* Keep the banned option token out of the lakefile comment

The lake-options quality check scans the raw lakefile text, comments
included.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;

* Keep warning policy compatible with proof-length documentation

---------

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
