  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/6c34d3481b31b819f945f9f0e86b0ff15ed659fd</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/LeanPool/lean-pool/commit/6c34d3481b31b819f945f9f0e86b0ff15ed659fd"/>
    <title>
        Restore the merge queue&#39;s build on main after a toolchain bump (#740)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T01:02:56Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17322558?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>Vilin97</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/Vilin97</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Restore the merge queue&amp;#39;s build on main after a toolchain bump (#740)

* Restore the merge queue&amp;#39;s build on main after a toolchain bump

Main cannot read caches saved by merge-queue runs. After a Lean/Mathlib
bump (or a cache eviction) the push run therefore found no build cache and
rebuilt the whole pool in shards: 4.5h after #530, while PRs ran cold too.

A merge-queue build that starts cold now also uploads its full build as
the existing lean-pool-build artifact. When the main push run is cold, the
planner checks whether the green queue run for that exact commit published
one; if so it plans a single job that restores it, verifies the tree and
pins, replays Lake, and saves main&amp;#39;s cache. Any miss falls back to the
ordinary build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;

* Fall back to a sharded rebuild when the queue build cannot be restored

The planner trades the sharded plan for the restore, so a failed download
would leave one job compiling the whole pool. Record the planner&amp;#39;s choice
as an output and, if the restore fails, dispatch a force_full sharded run
and stop this job.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;

* Free runner disk before Exposition Verify restores the pool build

The dependency and pool build caches no longer fit in the runner&amp;#39;s
default free space, so the verify job died with ENOSPC while restoring
them in the merge queue. Lean Action CI already frees the same paths.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;

---------

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
