  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/bc7dbb3a8841a7bd19b7627e6151a09e64412b2a</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/LeanPool/lean-pool/commit/bc7dbb3a8841a7bd19b7627e6151a09e64412b2a"/>
    <title>
        Eichler-Shimura material from FLT (#696)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-11-05T12:27:54Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3439688?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>loefflerd</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/loefflerd</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Eichler-Shimura material from FLT (#696)

* Eichler-Shimura material from FLT

* Clarify Eichler-Shimura assumptions and expose the project entry

Retain applicable upstream attribution; preserve every mathematical source file.

* extend Hecke equivariance

* Expose the unconditional Eichler-Shimura headline from the project entry

Refresh the generated project card and retain all author proof changes and attribution.

* fix unused-variable warnings, tighten up main results

* typo

* Lots of code improvements

* Add more top-level theorems, reimplement P2MUtil to avoid `modifyScope`

* remove heartbeat bumps

* Add missing headers

* shorten long proofs

* Shorten 3 more long proofs

* Remove long proofs over 200 lines

* Fix files failing the &amp;quot;long proof&amp;quot; script (all false positives)

* use fewer main decls

* shake imports

* Fix unused arguments and simp normal-form lint

* remove lint

* update attributions

* remove redundant material

* Correct constant-extension and elliptic-quotient citation scope

Correct Stichtenoth 3.6.3(d) references and distinguish the current constant-extension hypotheses. Describe the cyclic-kernel argument as a consequence of the stated endomorphism hypothesis, with Silverman III.4.12 cited for quotient/isogeny background. Documentation only; all mathematical statements, proofs, imports and quality gates are unchanged.

* simplification

* Rebase to Mathlib 4.35.0

* reinstate longer list of main decls

* correct wording in YAML file

---------

Co-authored-by: Vasily Ilin &amp;lt;vasilin97@gmail.com&amp;gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
